0 cm I.D.); mobile phase: PBS-buffer (pH 7.4), flow rate: 1.0 mL/min; detector: ICP-AES at 193.091 nm; injection volume: 20 <italic>&#x003bc;</italic>L.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BCA2008-539082.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>The superimposed chromatograms of AsB, As(III), MMA  (III), and DMA(III) as a function of the SEC column temperature at 4&#x000b0;C (&#x02014;), 25&#x000b0;C (- - -), or 37&#x000b0;C (&#x02013; &#x02013; &#x02013;). Stationary phase: Sephadex G-15 (31 &#x000d7; 1.0 cm I.D.); mobile phase: PBS buffer containing 10 mM GSH adjusted to pH 7.4, flow rate: 1.0 mL/min; detector: ICP-AES at 189.042 nm; injection volume: 20 <italic>&#x003bc;</italic>L (10 <italic>&#x003bc;</italic>g As per compound).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BCA2008-539082.003"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>